    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Brahmo Samaj spearheaded early intellectual reform, advocating monotheism and the abolition of social evils like Sati.",
        "Arya Samaj advocated a revivalist approach based on Vedic authority, promoting social service and educational institutions.",
        "Aligarh Movement sought to modernize Muslim society through Western education and scientific rationalism.",
        "Ramakrishna Mission synthesized Indian spirituality with selfless service to humanity (Practical Vedanta).",
        "Legislative reforms targeting women's rights, such as widow remarriage and child marriage restriction, formed the bedrock of social progress."
      ],
      "id": "r4wwas5"
    },
